#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# poset_moebius_mu

#% text
# `poset_moebius_mu(P, x, y)`: the Moebius function of the poset; poset_moebius_mu(P): its matrix

#% section
# Details

#% item
# A poset is `poset(elements, relations)`: relations are pairs [a, b] meaning a <= b (closed under reflexivity and transitivity), or a function f with f(a, b) true when a <= b.

#% item
# On the divisors ordered by divisibility the Moebius function is the number-theoretic one.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
d = poset(divisors(12), (a, b) => mod(b, a) == 0); poset_moebius_mu(d, 1, 12)
#% output
#= 0

#% cell
map(x => poset_moebius_mu(d, 1, x), divisors(12))
#% output
#= [1, -1, -1, 0, 1, 0]

#% cell
poset_moebius_mu(poset([1, 2, 3], [[1, 2], [1, 3]]))
#% output
#= [[1, -1, -1], [0, 1, 0], [0, 0, 1]]

